MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- the weighted candidate pass takes N, alias grades and the canonical
  observation from the published registry view, so a caller's filtered
  list cannot inflate a domain's share or hide a proven alias; the
  single-DS verdict is exact and cheap (O(rows))
- ds_cache_invalidate keeps each DS's capacity record and republishes
  the view; the create boundary also reads DS admin state live
- placement_admit feeds per-DS rejection reasons into
  pnfs_mds_placement_rejections_total; alias grades log an ERROR
- a mount path that is not a mount point is a failed probe for the
  background sweep (ds_capacity_probe_once_ex)
- placement_* numbers are parsed strictly; the generation covers
  ds_capacity_poll_ms; the last placement_domain_weight.<d> key wins
- tokens are refused after two publishes; domain_weight has the
  >184 EiB guard
- legacy promotion keeps the upstream by-value stripe count; the
  lookup WARN keeps the upstream prefix

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
